<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN BANKS TO RAISE INVESTMENT CREDIT RATES.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN BANKS TO RAISE INVESTMENT CREDIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian banks Generale Bank and Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA announced separately on Tuesday that they would raise the interest rate charged on investment loans with effect from Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rates for three-, five- and 10-year loans would rise to 5.70 percent, 6.60 percent and 7.75 percent from respectively 5.55 percent, 6.40 percent and 7.45 percent.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
